{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57865","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67082","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-57866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67083","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-67084","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-67085","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-67086","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-67087","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-67088","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-57867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67089","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57868","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67090","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-57869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67091","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-67092","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-67093","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-57870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67094","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-67095","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-57871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67096","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-67097","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-67098","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-57872","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-57873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67099","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57874","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67100","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-57875","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-57876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67101","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57877","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67102","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-57878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67103","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-57879","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67104","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-57880","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67105","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-67106","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-67107","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-57881","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67108","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-57883","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67109","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-57885","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67110","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-57887","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67111","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-57889","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57891","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67112","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-57892","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67113","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-67114","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-67115","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-57893","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67116","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-67117","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-57895","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67118","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-57897","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67119","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-57899","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67120","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-57901","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67121","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-57903","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67122","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57906","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67123","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-57907","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67124","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-67125","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-67126","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-57908","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-57909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67127","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57910","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67128","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-57911","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67129","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-57912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67130","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67131","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-67132","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67133","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-67134","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57913","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57915","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67135","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-67136","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-67137","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67138","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-67139","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67140","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-67141","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-57914","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67142","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-57916","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67143","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-67144","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-67145","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-57918","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67146","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-67147","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-67148","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-57920","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67149","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-67150","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-67151","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-67152","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-57922","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67153","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-67154","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-67155","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67156","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-67157","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57925","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67158","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-57926","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67159","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-57928","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67160","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-57930","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67161","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-67162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-67163","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67164","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-67165","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57933","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57935","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67166","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-67167","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-57934","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57937","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67168","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-67169","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-57936","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67170","text":"4. "},{"id":"spn-67171","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-67172","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]},{"id":"blk-57939","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67173","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-57940","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67174","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-57941","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67175","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-67176","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-67177","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67178","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-67179","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-57942","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57944","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67180","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-67181","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-67182","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-67183","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-57943","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67184","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-67185","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-67186","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-57945","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57948","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67187","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-67188","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-67189","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-67190","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-57947","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57950","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67191","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-67192","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-67193","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-67194","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-57949","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57952","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67195","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-67196","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-57951","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57954","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67197","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-67198","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-57953","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57956","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67199","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-67200","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-57955","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57958","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67201","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-67202","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-57957","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57960","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67203","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-67204","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-57959","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57962","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67205","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-67206","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-57961","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57964","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67207","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-67208","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-67209","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-57963","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67210","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-67211","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-67212","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-57965","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67213","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-67214","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-67215","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-57967","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67216","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-67217","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-57970","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67218","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-67219","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-57971","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67220","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-67221","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-57973","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67222","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-67223","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-57975","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67224","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-57977","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67225","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-67226","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-67227","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agentelic or the user's own API key) processes. SpecPrompt is a tool, not an agent. The MCP server version ("},{"id":"spn-67228","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-67229","text":") returns the prompt for the agent t